     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Raju heard Tamil patriots sung about in a song. \"Who fought for freedom in Tamil Nadu?\" he asked."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "V. O. Chidambaram Pillai",
     "Bharati",
     "Vedaranyam Salt March",
     "Rajaji",
     "Tiruppur Kumaran",
     "Kamaraj"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Tamil Nadu played a big part in the freedom struggle. V. O. Chidambaram Pillai started the Swadeshi Steam Navigation Company at Thoothukudi to challenge British shipping. Subramania Bharati inspired people with patriotic songs.\nSubramania Siva, Vanchinathan, who killed the collector Ashe, and Vanchi Aiyar were revolutionaries. S. Satyamurti and Rajaji led the Congress, and the Vedaranyam Salt March of 1930 led by Rajaji was held in the Cauvery delta.\nWomen like Dr Muthulakshmi Reddy, Rukmini Lakshmipathi, Ambujammal and Vedaratnam took part, and Tiruppur Kumaran gave his life with the national flag. Kamaraj, a leader of the Congress, later became a great Chief Minister."
    }
   },
